<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Taizu of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1068">1068</a>–1123</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wanyan Aguda, Aguda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wanyan Aguda was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> and its first emperor, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Taizu</a>, ruling from 1115 to 1123. Chief of the Wanyan clan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, he rebelled against the Khitan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> in 1114, proclaimed the Jin in 1115 and won a series of victories that brought down the Liao, completed by his brother after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-jin.jpg" alt="Emperor Taizu of Jin" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wanggiyan_Aguda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Resentment of Liao demands, including tribute in hunting falcons and the abuse of Jurchen communities by Liao envoys, led the Wanyan chief <b>Aguda</b> to rebel in 1114.</blockquote><a href="/empire/jin-dynasty-1115-1234">Jin dynasty (1115-1234) · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1114 the Jurchen chieftain <b>Wanyan Aguda</b> rebelled and defeated Liao forces at Ningjiang, and in 1115 he proclaimed the Jin dynasty; later that year his small army routed a far larger force led by Tianzuo at Hubudagang.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>At the end of 1122 the Jurchen ruler <b>Aguda</b> took Yanjing with little resistance; Xiao Defei fled and was later killed by Tianzuo.</blockquote><a href="/state/northern-liao">Northern Liao</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Acheng District, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.54,126.97&amp;year=1103" aria-label="Acheng District on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7561 558 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Emperor Taizu of Jin"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8011 828h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8011 828h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.54,126.97&amp;year=1103">What was here in 1103? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
